{"candidateAnswer":"Deborah uses daily schedules and to-do lists; Jolene uses Pomodoro Technique and bullet journaling.","evidence":"[D10:4 | 5:35 pm on 22 March, 2023] Jolene: I'm using the Pomodoro Technique - 25 minutes work, 5-minute break - to avoid burnout but I'm still struggling to prioritize. Do you have any other tips on time management?\n[D10:5 | 5:35 pm on 22 March, 2023] Deborah: I create a daily schedule or to-do list. Here's my example for today.\n[D10:6 | 5:35 pm on 22 March, 2023] Jolene: I tried making one but it's kinda overwhelming when it's a big stack of tasks. Here's an example from last Friday.\n[D10:13 | 5:35 pm on 22 March, 2023] Deborah: The Eisenhower Matrix sorts tasks into four boxes, categorizing them based on their urgency and importance. It can be really useful for organizing and prioritizing. Here's a breakdown. \n[D18:3 | 2:58 pm on 16 August, 2023] Jolene: Thanks, Deb! I've been trying out some time management strategies recently and started using a bullet journal. It's been really helpful for tracking my tasks and staying organized.","itemId":"urn:uuid:28b65cac-5635-5ab8-b7b0-1a2ef56c2c89","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:15a712eca56c1f71c0d800a8ee6df12e78909f9a10a81b8b6dc7857ac924d9b9","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What time management techniques do Deborah and Jolene use?","referenceAnswer":"the Pomodoro Technique - 25 minutes work and 5-minute break, scheduler or to-do list, The Eisenhower Matrix, bullet journal","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"15a712eca56c1f71c0d800a8ee6df12e78909f9a10a81b8b6dc7857ac924d9b9"}}]}